  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: labels only. Change ONLY the three button/tile labels named below + the tests that assert their accessible names. Do NOT change onClick handlers, routing, apply/dismiss logic, testids, or add surfaces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="UX-§E">E1a: EmailConnectionsReview create-new tile label "Create new record" → "New record", rendered in the "+ {verb}" consistency form ("+ New record") with an Add icon (AddRegular / Add16Regular) matching the "+ New task" button in TaskReconcileTab. If the tile is a link-card (span label, not a Button), keep its structure — just set the label text + ensure the add/plus affordance is visible.</constraint>
    <constraint source="UX-§E">E2a: verify FieldUpdateReconcileTab proposal primary already reads "Accept". If it already does, make NO change (it does at authoring time, ~line 440). Do not restyle.</constraint>
    <constraint source="UX-§E">E3a: TaskReconcileTab proposal primary button (data-testid="task-reconcile-accept", ~line 606) text "Accept" → "Create". Keep the testid, icon, appearance, and onClick unchanged. NOTE the divergence: the shipped component had unified on "Accept"; this restores the owner's explicit E3a wording. The "+ New task" ad-hoc FormModal submitLabel ("Create task") is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens only; reuse the existing AddRegular icon import already present in TaskReconcileTab for the E1a icon (import into EmailConnectionsReview from @fluentui/react-icons if not already imported).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-050/012">Do not change modal chrome or component contracts — text + icon only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: no deploy. Build + test only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

