  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Load this POML + UX §E. Re-grep the three current labels to confirm live state (they may have shifted since authoring): EmailConnectionsReview create tile, FieldUpdateReconcileTab Accept, TaskReconcileTab proposal primary. Run /conflict-check (shared Communication.Components).</step>
    <step order="1">E1a: in EmailConnectionsReview.tsx, set the create-new tile label to "New record" in the "+ New record" consistency form + ensure an Add icon renders (match the "+ New task" pattern). Preserve the tile's gated-by-onCreateNewRecord structure.</step>
    <step order="2">E2a: verify FieldUpdateReconcileTab proposal primary reads "Accept" — if already correct, no change.</step>
    <step order="3">E3a: in TaskReconcileTab.tsx, change the proposal-primary button text "Accept" → "Create" (testid/icon/onClick unchanged).</step>
    <step order="4">Update tests: TaskReconcileTab.test.tsx assertions on the proposal button's accessible name (Accept → Create); any EmailConnectionsReview test asserting the create-tile label. Keep all other assertions intact.</step>
    <step order="5">Build the shared lib green (tsc 0-err) + run the affected jest suites (TaskReconcileTab, FieldUpdateReconcileTab, EmailConnectionsReview) — all green.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: add/confirm 063 row → ✅. Note the E3a "Accept"→"Create" divergence in notes/063-*.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If E2a is NOT already "Accept" (shipped state shifted), STOP and report — the reconciliation table in this POML assumed the shipped state; a mismatch means the UX §E table needs re-checking before proceeding.</trigger>
    <trigger>If changing the Tasks proposal to "Create" breaks a routing/semantic assumption in the tests beyond the label (e.g., a test keys off the word "Accept" for behavior, not just display), STOP and surface it — the E3a rename may need an owner call on consistency vs. explicit wording.</trigger>
